    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35545" root="قرظ" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَقْرُوظٌ</span></b>  A skin, or hide, <i>tanned with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرَظ</span>; (S,
Msb, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرَظِىٌّ</span></b> ; and AHn mentions,
on the authority of Aboo-Mis-hal, ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُقْرَظٌ</span></b> , as
though from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقْرَظَهُ</span>, which, he says, we have not
heard: (TA:) or <i>dyed therewith.</i> (K.)

